    "created_at": "2026-07-04T11:25:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-04T11:25:47Z",
    "body": "You can do this today with `hyprland/workspaces` + `workspace-taskbar` and `active-only: true`, which limits the window buttons to the currently active workspace (see the example posted by @codevogel in this thread, and `populateWorkspaceTaskbarConfig` in src/modules/hyprland/workspaces.cpp; also available for niri). The generic `wlr/taskbar` protocol has no notion of workspaces, so per-workspace filtering has to come from a compositor-specific module like this one. Closing as answered 🙏 — reopen if you need this on a compositor that lacks such a module.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
